Q: How do I make this code shorter and more efficient? A: <p>In analyzing the code and taking into account the length of time that has passed, it seemed appropriate to offer up some possible code refactoring to streamline the code and to add some clarification to the refactored bits.  With that, following is one such refactoring scenario that includes some comments on the refactoring.</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#include &lt;cs50.h&gt;
#include &lt;stdbool.h&gt;

int check_length(long);
void check_company(long, int);
bool check_luhn(long);

int main(void)
{
    int length;     /* Define length within function - avoid using global variables when possible   */

    long cc = get_long(&quot;Enter Credit Card Number: &quot;);

    length = check_length(cc);

    if(check_luhn(cc))
    {
        check_company(cc, length);
    }
    else
    {
        printf(&quot;INVALID CARD NUMBER\n&quot;);
    }
}

int check_length(long cc)
{
    int len = 0;

    while (cc &gt; 0)
    {
        cc /= 10;
        len++;
    }
    return len;
}

void check_company(long cc, int len)
{
    int digit1, digit2;

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; len - 2; i++)   /* Divide by &quot;10&quot; until under &quot;100&quot; */
        cc /= 10;

    digit1 = cc / 10;
    digit2 = cc % 10;

    if((len == 15) &amp;&amp; ((digit1 == 3) &amp;&amp; ((digit2 == 4) || digit2 == 7)))
    {
        printf(&quot;AMEX\n&quot;);
    }
    else if(((len == 13) || (len == 16)) &amp;&amp; (digit1 == 4))
    {
        printf(&quot;VISA\n&quot;);
    }
    else if((len == 16) &amp;&amp; (digit1 == 5) &amp;&amp; ((digit2 &gt;= 1) &amp;&amp; (digit2) &lt;= 5))
    {
        printf(&quot;MASTERCARD\n&quot;);
    }
    else
    {
        printf(&quot;UNKNOWN ISSUER\n&quot;); /* Fallback - card issuer is unknown                */
    }
}

bool check_luhn(long cc)
{
    bool odd = true;            /* Odd/even digit conditional check flag                */
    int digit, sum = 0;

    while (cc &gt; 0)              /* Effectively reads cc number from right to left       */
    {
        digit = cc % 10;        /* Evaluate the current right most digit                */

        if (odd)
        {
            sum += digit;       /* Odd numbered digit values added to working summary   */
            odd = false;        /* Alternate the odd/even flag                          */
        }
        else
        {
            digit *= 2;         /* Even numbered digits are doubled then checked        */

            if (digit &gt; 9)      /* If greater than &quot;9&quot; subtract &quot;9&quot; from the value      */
                digit -= 9;     /* Effectively the same as adding the digits            */

            sum += digit;
            odd = true;         /* Alternate the odd/even flag                          */
        }

        cc /= 10;               /* Move onto the next digit                             */
    }

    if (sum % 10 == 0)
        return true;
    else
        return false;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Following were some tests with fictional credit card numbers.  Some would be valid while others would not be valid or not pertain to a credit card issuer.</p>
<pre><code>craig@Vera:~/C_Programs/Console/CS50_Luhn3/bin/Release$ ./CS50_Luhn3 
